<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Diaspora.Modules.Financial</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Diaspora.Modules.Financial</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The Financial Platform, Wallet &amp; Monetization Engine (Phase B15). The platform's single
      owner of every financial concept: financial identity, wallets, the immutable ledger, payment
      intents, transactions, refunds, credits, promotions, subscriptions, monetization products,
      placements, donations, community contributions, platform revenue and financial policy.

      This is not a payment gateway integration. It is the ledger-first financial substrate every
      other module requests capabilities from. No business module owns payment logic, wallet logic
      or ledger logic; a vertical that wants to sell something declares a monetization product and
      consumes a published contract.

      What Financial owns: the wallet projection, the append-only ledger the projection is derived
      from, the payment-intent lifecycle, the transaction record, the versioned financial-policy
      catalogue, the monetization-product catalogue, subscriptions, promotions and coupons, credit
      grants, donations, community contributions, purchased placements, and the revenue rollups.
      What it deliberately does not own: any business data. There is no listing, job, property,
      provider or event in this schema — only a subject reference (type + identifier) that names
      something in somebody else's module, which this module never resolves.

      The ledger is append-only and the wallet is a projection of it. There is no code path
      anywhere on the platform that sets a balance; balances move because entries are appended, and
      an architecture test asserts the aggregate exposes no balance setter.

      Payment providers are abstractions. IPaymentGateway, IPaymentWebhookProcessor and
      IPaymentReconciliationProvider have deterministic mock implementations behind them today and
      no vendor is named anywhere in the assembly. Stripe, Paystack, Flutterwave, Adyen, Telr,
      Peach Payments and manual transfer are all adapters this module has never heard of.

      Registers entirely through B2.6 contributor interfaces: no edit to the Platform Kernel, to
      any previously completed module, or to Program.cs.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The same narrow reference set B13 and B14 established, and for the same reason. The Financial
    Platform consumes published contracts and nothing else, so it references Diaspora.Contracts for
    the events it subscribes to and takes no ProjectReference on Identity, Trust, Community,
    Providers, Guides, Jobs, Marketplace, Housing, Community Life, Notifications or Recommendations
    at all. A paid placement on a marketplace listing is a subject reference and a purchase; if the
    payload of a published contract is not enough, the fix is to enrich the contract, never to reach
    into the module.

    Diaspora.Application is referenced for the CQRS abstractions and the integration-event handler
    base; Diaspora.Persistence for IDatabaseContributor and the shared context. Architecture tests
    enforce the absence of every module reference.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.SharedKernel\Diaspora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Contracts\Diaspora.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Platform\Diaspora.Platform.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Application\Diaspora.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Persistence\Diaspora.Persistence.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
